  "reviewer_notes": "One application (single wet-process cement plant, Colombia). Four energy performance constructs were separated as models: M1 the linear energy baseline (E = mP + Enap), M2 the specific Energy Consumption Indicator (intensity ratio), M3 the Percent Energy Efficiency Indicator (composite index), and M4 the CUSUM control chart. No numeric baseline coefficients or fit statistics for this plant are reported. The 7.0/9.1 kWh/ton savings potentials are attributed to M1 (derived from baseline/target-line analysis); the achieved 4.6%/5.2 kWh/ton reduction and CO2 result are attributed to M4 (demonstrated via the CUSUM chart). K2 (Enap as non-productive/baseload energy) is offered with requires inference as it explains the indicator design rather than being framed by the authors as a limitation.",
